  "term": "narcotic",
  "definition": "A narcotic is an opioid-type drug, often synthetic and similar to opium-derived substances, that has pain-relieving effects. It works by attaching to opiate receptors and producing opiate-like effects on nerve cells and other body cells, influencing pain and behavior.",
